<BaseLayout title="About Doug & Tara | Rise After Nest" description="Meet Doug and Tara Markott, the empty nesters behind Rise After Nest."><Header /><main><section class="about-hero"><div><span class="script">Hi, we’re Doug &amp; Tara</span><h1>The nest is empty.<br/>The story is just getting good.</h1><p>We’re a married team learning how much possibility can fit into the years after raising a family.</p></div><div class="about-stack"><figure class="polaroid"><img src={photos.coast} alt="A scenic mountain lake"/><figcaption>more room to wander</figcaption></figure><figure class="polaroid"><img src="/images/nassau-diver.jpg" alt="Tara diving in Nassau"/><figcaption>still trying new things ♡</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="page-section about-story"><div><span class="kicker">WHY RISE AFTER NEST?</span><h2>We didn’t want “empty nest” to sound like an ending.</h2></div><div><p>For years, schedules, school, and family shaped the map. We loved that chapter. Now the calendar looks different, and we’re learning to fill it with shared stories.</p><p>Rise After Nest is where we keep those stories: the places that surprised us, the honest details that help someone else plan, and the reminder that curiosity doesn’t have an expiration date.</p><blockquote>“The kids have their adventures. These are ours.”</blockquote></div></section><section class="values-strip"><article><span>01</span><h3>Travel together</h3><p>The point is the time we share.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Tell the truth</h3><p>Useful details beat polished perfection.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Stay curious</h3><p>There’s always another first ahead.</p></article></section></main><Footer /></BaseLayout>
